Nowadays I think it is.  When I started playing, I thought different :)
After I lost a *lot* of promising (eh, aren't they all? :) characters,
I learned not to do this.  I can't remember the last time it happened
to me.  I treat floating eyes with *extreme* caution now.

That's just the way of nethack.  You don't pay attention, you die. You
get brave, you die.  You get cowardly, you die too :)

I think the nethack motto should be: "to die and to learn".

So put on a brave face, and get on hacking! You have to play a lot
for these things to become reflexes.  Hell, when I *type* nowadays (I mean
letters, documents, programs) every once in a while I get a scare when I
look at the screen and see certain combinations of letters, or some letters
in isolation.  Things like: I thinking about life, then look at the
screen and see a " c ".  Immediately the alarm sirens start at full power,
"Cockatrice Alert!!! Attention!!!".  Well, you get the point.  You are not
playing enough if this does not happen to you.

Good luck!
